  "summary": "composite and record values now read as labelled sub-values on the record page instead of raw JSON. In packages/fields/src/index.tsx, buildStandardCellRendererMap maps composite to CompositeCellRenderer and record to RecordMapCellRenderer. Both are module-local and share StructuredValueCell, beside JsonCellRenderer; json and object keep JsonCellRenderer. Composite draws `Width 10 · Height 20`. Record draws one labelled group per entry, `Primary (Name A · Score 9) · Backup (Name B · Score 7)`, and a scalar entry as a pair. A number sub-value goes through formatNumberFieldValue with no scale, a boolean through useBooleanValueLabel (the existing common.yes / common.no keys), a string as itself, and a floor member as EmptyValue. A nested object or array stays compact JSON through a new compactJsonText helper, which is JsonCellRenderer's own stringify moved out with the same bytes. The face is one truncated line (`block max-w-full truncate`) with the full text in its title. It is a description list, and the separators and brackets are aria-hidden. The floor, [], {} and non-object values (a JSON string included) still go to JsonCellRenderer, so the objectui#8474 and #8481 fence pins pass unedited. DetailSection.tsx is untouched: the record page row already draws one truncated line with a title, so the cell contract expresses this face. Zone 2 hypotheses: (1) the path is confirmed by ablation. (2) No sub-field declaration reaches the renderer. On installed @objectstack/spec 17.6.0, FieldSchema.safeParse refuses `fields` and `subFields` on a composite field as unrecognized_keys. The control relatedListColumns parses. The 75-key shape has no fields, subFields, schema or itemSchema, and objectstack main 60ccda5a is the same. objectui's FieldMetadata union has no composite or record member, and ObjectFieldMetadata.schema exists only for type 'object'. So labels are humanizeLabel(key), and no spec declaration was added. (3) The Field Zoo seeds are the fixtures. The driver-sql and dogfood shape `{home,work}` (scalar record entries) is pinned as pairs. (4) humanizeLabel from core is the in-package key fallback; humanizeFieldKey (camelCase split) lives in plugin-dashboard, outside this package's dependency edge. (5) The address precedent was followed. Raw view: none existed and none was added. The record page copy button still copies the stored JSON, because composite and record are inline-excluded. The Done-when clause \"through the field metadata\" cannot be met on the current spec, because the spec has no sub-field declaration. That is reported below as a finding with a Seam line, per Zone 3.",
  "tests": "All at HEAD 22274e7. FULL: `pnpm exec vitest run packages/fields/ --maxWorkers=2` gave Test Files 238 passed | 1 skipped (239), Tests 3723 passed | 7 skipped (3730), exit 0. `pnpm exec vitest run packages/plugin-detail/ --maxWorkers=2` gave Test Files 245 passed | 1 skipped (246), Tests 2408 passed | 8 skipped (2416), exit 0. Both ran in one os-verify-lock run, each part's exit echoed separately: PD_EXIT=0, FIELDS_EXIT=0. NEW PINS: packages/fields/src/__tests__/compositeRecordCell-11697.test.tsx has 9 tests. They cover composite pairs, record groups, scalar record entries, nested JSON, the per-type sub-value faces (number compared against the number cell's own text: 1,234.5; Yes / No; the No value affordance), the one-line contract with the title equal to the text, the unchanged floor and fallbacks ([], {}, a JSON string never parsed), and the json / object control. packages/plugin-detail/src/__tests__/DetailSection.compositeRecord-11697.test.tsx has 2 tests: the triage pin, a composite field renders labelled sub-values on the record page, plus the record field. MOVED PINS: AddressCellRenderer.test.tsx's JSON control now lists json and object only. The summaryChip.badgeFitCensus-8464 composite and record rows now read `Id acct-1 · Name Acme Corp`, still fit. The first full fields run on the fix commit 9159c55, before any pin moved, showed exactly 1 red (Tests 1 failed | 3713 passed): the address control naming composite and record as JSON. ABLATION, after committing the fix: `node /home/user/objectstack/scripts/ablation-replace.mjs` replaced the two table entries with JsonCellRenderer (anchor x1 -> x0, replacement x0 -> x1, blob 6e801a91c25e -> ff9c729d76ec). On disk, grep -c counted `composite: JsonCellRenderer` 1 and `composite: CompositeCellRenderer` 0. The two new pin files then gave Tests 8 failed | 3 passed (11). All 6 contract tests and both record-page pins went red. The 3 green tests are the floor and fallback cases and the json / object control