  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Triage's Done-when asks for sub-field labels \"through the field metadata\". The spec has no sub-field declaration for composite or record: FieldSchema refuses fields and subFields. Should one be added so labels come from metadata?",
      "options": [
        "A: no declaration now. Labels stay humanized keys (what this PR ships). The FieldType enum comment \"with declared sub-fields\" is reworded only if a carrier touches field.zod.ts.",
        "B: add a sub-field member to FieldSchema for composite and record (name, label, type), have the renderer read labels from it, and enforce values against it at write and publish time."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A. Real business need: the measured producers are the showcase Field Zoo (type and label only) and two test fixtures, and none of them declares or wants sub-fields, so there is zero pull. Long-term soundness: a declaration belongs with enforcement (value validation against the sub-fields). A label-only member would be a capability declared but not enforced, which is the shape enforce-or-remove retires. Preventing AI mistakes: today an AI that writes `fields` on a composite field is refused loudly at parse, which is the correct strictness, while a label-only member would accept sub-field types and requirements that nothing enforces. Startup-stage scope: no pull means no new declaration surface. The four axes do not conflict."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "class: b (candidate, below the filing bar) · reach: NOT MEASURED at a public door. The reading is schema-level only: installed @objectstack/spec 17.6.0 FieldSchema.safeParse({name, type: 'composite', label, fields: [...]}) refuses `fields`, and `subFields` likewise, as unrecognized_keys, while the control relatedListColumns parses. No real producer was found · evidence: the objectstack spec FieldType enum comment reads 'composite' = \"Single embedded sub-object with declared sub-fields\" and 'repeater' = \"Repeating embedded sub-object array with declared sub-fields\", while the FieldSchema key set has no sub-field member · Seam: spec:FieldType 'composite' / 'record' (enum comment 'with declared sub-fields') → runtime: FieldSchema key set (no sub-field member; fields / subFields refused) | renderer: getCellRenderer('composite' / 'record') StructuredValueCell (labels = humanizeLabel(key)) · reported per dispatch Zone 3, not filed · dedupe words: composite declared sub-fields, FieldSchema subFields composite, composite record sub-field labels, embedded sub-object field schema",
